{"n": 11, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "11.webp", "text": "00-4\n\nGeneral Information\nBMW MAINTENANCE SYSTEM\n\nTechnical Nominal\n\n0000009 Pre-delivery inspection Important Intormation!\n\nCheck operation of engine, clutch, transmission, tinal drive,\nSteering, foot and hand operated brakes. Cars with rear disc\nbrakes: break In parking brake.\n\nCheck function of speedometer with odometer and daily trip\nrecorder, t (Economy Control), clock, temperature\nand tuet gages.\n\nCheck engino, transmission, steering, final drive, dust covers\non drive shatts, fuel, clutch and brake systems for leaks.\n\nRemove seat and other protective covers.\nReset the service indicator\n\nimportant!\nThe service indicator (SI) must be reset atter completion of the\npre-delivery inspection as follows.\nSwitch oft all electrical equipment.\nTurn on ignition; do not run engine.\nPlug S-R* with adapter’ for large (20-pin) diagnosis socket in\ndiagnosis socket.\n\nPush In and hold recessed, red INSPECTION button - green\nlamp (function control) comes on.\n\nRed lamp also comes on after approx. 3 sec. and goes out\natter approx. 12 seconds.\n\nRelease inspection button - green lamp goes out.\n\nGradual Introduction of new SI display with clock symbol and\nonly one ced diode light since January, 1986. Load snd time\nmemories are separated.and resetting must be repeated to\nreset the time memory. The break betore the second inspection\nreset must be at least 10 seconds long, but may be up to 17.5\nhours after the first reset,\n\nCheck Service indicator Display\n\nAll tive green diode lights must be on.\n\nYellow and possibly red diode lights as well as INSPECTION\nsign should go out.\n\n* SR = Service Indicator Resetter, Order No. 62 1 100\n“* Adapter, Order No. 62 1 140.", "words": [["00-4", 0.4554, 0.0371, 0.5203, 0.0564], ["General", 0.5299, 0.1081, 0.5694, 0.118], ["Information", 0.5735, 0.1088, 0.6312, 0.118], ["BMW", 0.0628, 0.124, 0.0876, 0.134], ["MAINTENANCE", 0.0917, 0.1233, 0.169